{"resourceIdentifier":"3797","resourceName":"Ödemis Integrated Solid Waste Management Plant","description":"The Ödemis Integrated Waste Management Plant (IWMP) started operation in 2020 and was designed to receive all the municipal waste from the Districts of Ödemiş, Kiraz, Beydağ, Bayındır, Tire, Selcuk and Torbalı. It aimed to revolutionise waste management practices in Turkey. The Plant accepts three types of waste: Mixed municipal solid waste (MSW), Domestic bulky waste, and Other biodegradable wastes (i.e. parks&gardens, forestry and agricultural residues). In the ISWMP, the mixed municipal waste goes through a material recovery facility to remove the greater flow of recyclable materials, while the organic fragment undergoes biological treatment. Three anaerobic digesters are currently in operation for processing the organic waste, with a capacity of 400 tons each, resulting in high-quality fertiliser products. The designed maximum capacity of the Plant for the year 2050 is around 360,000 tons/y. The main goal was to divert at least 55% of the input waste into valuable products such as Plastic packaging material such as paper and cardboard, Glass and Metals.","location":{"latitude":38.198300,"longitude":27.960300},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-10-28","endExclusive":"2022-11-28","endInclusive":"2022-11-27"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3797"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"İzmir"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Biosun Ödemis Kati Atik İsleme Enerji ve Cevre San. Tic. A.S"},{"type":"string","value":"İZMİR, Turkey"},{"type":"string","value":"gultekinozkan@biosunas.com.tr"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3797"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values"